[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Output Buffering in PHP"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Output buffering is a mechanism in PHP that allows you to control when and how the output of your script is sent to the browser. By default, PHP sends output as it's generated. Output buffering lets you capture the output, modify it, and then send it all at once or discard it entirely."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Why Use Output Buffering?"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Headers: Modify HTTP headers after some output has already been generated (which is normally not allowed)."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Redirection: Perform redirects (using 'header()') after some output has been generated."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Content Manipulation: Modify the output before it's sent to the browser (e.g., compression, search and replace)."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Error Handling: Prevent partial output in case of errors; either send the complete output or nothing at all."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Output Buffering Functions"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"PHP provides several functions to manage output buffering:"},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'ob_start()': Starts output buffering. All output will be stored in an internal buffer instead of being sent to the browser."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'ob_get_contents()': Returns the contents of the output buffer."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'ob_end_clean()': Cleans (erases) the output buffer and turns off output buffering."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'ob_end_flush()': Flushes (sends) the output buffer and turns off output buffering."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'ob_get_length()': Returns the length of the output buffer."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'ob_get_level()': Returns the nesting level of the output buffering mechanism."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'ob_flush()': Flush the output buffer."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'ob_clean()': Clean (erase) the output buffer."},{"order":18,"type":"subheading","text":"Basic Usage Example"},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"<?php

ob_start();

echo "This is some output.";

$output = ob_get_contents();
ob_end_clean();

echo "<p>The output was: " . htmlspecialchars($output) . "</p>";

?>"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this example, 'ob_start()' starts the output buffer. The 'echo' statement sends its output to the buffer. 'ob_get_contents()' retrieves the buffer's content, and 'ob_end_clean()' clears the buffer and stops output buffering. Finally, the retrieved content is displayed, safely escaped using 'htmlspecialchars()'."},{"order":21,"type":"subheading","text":"Flushing the Buffer"},{"order":22,"type":"code","text":"<?php

ob_start();

echo "This is some output that will be flushed.";

ob_flush();

echo "This is more output.";

ob_end_flush();

?>"},{"order":23,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this example, 'ob_flush()' sends the current content of the buffer to the browser immediately, without ending the buffering. 'ob_end_flush()' sends the remaining buffer content and stops output buffering."},{"order":24,"type":"subheading","text":"Nesting Output Buffers"},{"order":25,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can nest output buffers, creating multiple layers of buffering. This can be useful for complex content manipulation."},{"order":26,"type":"code","text":"<?php

ob_start(); // Outer buffer

echo "Outer buffer content.";

  ob_start(); // Inner buffer
  echo "Inner buffer content.";
  $inner_content = ob_get_contents();
  ob_end_clean();

echo "<p>Inner content: " . htmlspecialchars($inner_content) . "</p>";

$output = ob_get_contents();
ob_end_flush();

echo "<p>Final output: " . htmlspecialchars($output) . "</p>";

?>"},{"order":27,"type":"subheading","text":"Output Buffering Configuration"},{"order":28,"type":"paragraph","text":"Output buffering can also be configured in 'php.ini' using the 'output_buffering' directive. Setting it to 'On' or a buffer size will enable output buffering automatically for all scripts."},{"order":29,"type":"paragraph","text":"Example: 'output_buffering = 4096' (buffer size in bytes)."},{"order":30,"type":"subheading","text":"Important Considerations"},{"order":31,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Performance: Excessive buffering can impact performance. Use it judiciously."},{"order":32,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Character Encoding: Be mindful of character encoding when manipulating buffered content. Use functions like 'mb_convert_encoding()' if necessary."},{"order":33,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Headers: Ensure headers are sent before flushing the buffer if you intend to modify them."}]
